{"profile":{"name":"Jaye Robinson","ward":"Ward 15, Don Valley West","bio":"Jaye Robinson (1962-2024) was first elected to Toronto City Council in 2010 and re-elected in 2014, 2018 and 2022, serving Don Valley West for nearly 14 years. Before entering municipal politics, she spent more than 20 years as a city civil servant, including as the City of Toronto's Director of Special Events, where she helped launch Nuit Blanche, Summerlicious and Winterlicious. She served as Chair of the Public Works and Infrastructure Committee (2014-2018), where she introduced Toronto's first Vision Zero Road Safety Plan, and as Chair of the Toronto Transit Commission (2018-2022). She died in office on May 16, 2024, after being diagnosed with breast cancer in 2019; the seat was filled by Rachel Chernos Lin in the November 2024 by-election.","committees":["Economic and Community Development Committee","North York Community Council"],"contact":{"email":"councillor_robinson@toronto.ca","phone":"416-395-6408"},"promises":[{"text":"Pledged to keep the next council focused on better delivery of core municipal services such as snow clearance, pothole repair and garbage pick-up, arguing 'the next City Council's focus should be on providing better value to Toronto taxpayers.'","source":"https://www.knowyourvote.to/don-valley-west"},{"text":"Pledged support for open tendering of city contracts as a fiscal measure, stating it 'would have saved $12-48 million per year' on taxes and spending.","source":"https://www.knowyourvote.to/don-valley-west"},{"text":"Signed the Toronto Environmental Alliance's 'Greener City for All' election pledge, committing to actions toward Toronto's 2025, 2030 and 2040 climate targets, including fully funding the city's climate strategy and accelerating investments in affordable housing, transit and green jobs.","source":"https://www.torontoenvironment.org/2022_election_greener_city_pledge_results"}]},"lobbying":{"total":875,"term":64,"first":"2011-01-17","last":"2024-05